### Error handling

Throw a plain `Error` with a clear message. Avoid adding new entries to `ErrorCode`
(`lib/error_code.ts`) and `lib/constants/error_messages.js`.

We are moving toward a new design where the driver exposes a small set of error groups instead of a
unique code for every error. For now, just throw plain errors - they will be sorted into those
groups later.

❌

```typescript
throw createInvalidParameterError(ErrorCode.ERR_CONN_CREATE_INVALID_SOMETHING_NEW, someValue);
```

✅

```typescript
throw new Error(`Invalid something: ${someValue}. Expected ...`);
```
